  ('wizer-ctf-idor-task-manager-probe', 'generic', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'Wizer CTF Task Manager IDOR API exposed without auth',
   'Wizer CTF #11 Task Manager exposes POST /api/users and /api/tasks without authorization — sequential user_id enumeration enables cross-user task access.',
   'Public Wizer chal11 challenge returns unauthenticated JSON from /api/users and /api/tasks — IDOR training surface for sequential ID probing.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"wizerCtfIdorTaskManagerProbe"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Wizer CTF labs are intentional training — enforce object-level authorization on every API route in production.","steps":["Run Wizer CTF challenges only on isolated training infrastructure.","Verify the authenticated user owns the requested user_id before returning tasks.","Use non-enumerable IDs and server-side authorization checks on all object reads."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our Wizer-style task manager exposes /api/users and /api/tasks without auth checks. Show proper IDOR prevention patterns.',
   true),
  ('xpath-injection-disclosure', 'generic', 'Injection', 'high',
   'XPATH injection leaks credentials in XML response',
   'A login or search endpoint builds an XPATH query from user input. Boolean injection with '' or ''1''=''1 returns multiple <password> elements in the XML response — positive proof of credential disclosure.',
   'Attackers can extract other users'' passwords via XPATH injection.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"xpathInjectionDisclosure"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Parameterize XPATH queries; never concatenate user input.","steps":["Use XPATH variable bindings instead of string concatenation.","Validate and escape user input before query construction.","Return generic auth failures without leaking XML node data."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our /api/partners/partnerLogin endpoint is vulnerable to XPATH injection — password='' or ''1''=''1 returns multiple user passwords. Fix the XPATH query construction and show the patched handler.',
   true),
  ('xxe-xml-post-probe', 'generic', 'Injection', 'high',
   'XXE confirmed via POST XML entity expansion',
   'A server endpoint accepts POST application/xml and expands external entities in the response body. A live probe with a custom ENTITY canary echoed inside <root> proves XML External Entity processing.',
   'XXE lets attackers read local files, reach internal URLs, or trigger denial-of-service via entity expansion.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"xxeXmlPostProbe"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"_raw":"{ summary: \"Disable external entity processing in all XML parsers.\", steps: [ \"Reject DOCTYPE declarations and external entities in user-supplied XML.\", \"Set parser options: noent=false, nonet=true, dtdload=false.\", \"Return generic errors without echoing expanded entity content.\" ] }"}'::jsonb,
   'Our /api/metadata endpoint expands XML external entities on POST. Disable entity expansion, block DOCTYPE, and show the hardened parser configuration.',
   true)
